WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:03.060
Slaying zombies, directing movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:08.640
and looking fab. Dani is all grown up&nbsp;
and still showin' up. Forever and ever.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:14.760
Watching the 1993 film "Hocus Pocus" is&nbsp;
a requisite on Halloween. Not only is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:19.200
movie full of spooky fun, but it also&nbsp;
has plenty of heart. One of the film's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:25.200
most endearing characters is Dani, portrayed by&nbsp;
Thora Birch, the little sister of Max Dennison.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:27.300
"Boo!"

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.620
"Dani!"

00:00:29.869 --> 00:00:33.461
"I scared you. I scared you. Ah ha ha ha ha."

00:00:33.722 --> 00:00:37.620
In the film, Max begrudgingly goes&nbsp;
trick-or-treating with his sister and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:42.780
they end up at the Sanderson sisters' home,&nbsp;
where complete chaos ensues. With the help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:49.260
of the child-turned-black cat, Thackery Binx,&nbsp;
the zombie "Billy" Butcherson, and Max's crush,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:53.880
Allison, the siblings manage to escape&nbsp;
their encounter with the witches unscathed.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:01:00.840
During an October 2018 interview with People&nbsp;
magazine, the film's director Kenny Ortega briefly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:06.426
spoke about Thora Birch's performance as Dani&nbsp;
and couldn't stop gushing about her performance.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.720
"Thora Birch. One of the brightest&nbsp;
young children that, to this day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:13.151
that I've ever worked with. I mean&nbsp;
she was so ahead of the class."

00:01:13.151 --> 00:01:17.640
Birch also discussed her experience working&nbsp;
on "Hocus Pocus" while speaking to Access&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:24.360
in October 2018. Birch shared that she understood&nbsp;
the significance of acting alongside Bette Midler.

00:01:24.769 --> 00:01:31.021
"No, I was so excited. I mean, working with&nbsp;
her was like working with an idol of yours."

00:01:31.021 --> 00:01:36.240
After "Hocus Pocus" premiered, Thora Birch&nbsp;
appeared in a number of notable films including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:42.960
"Now and Then," "American Beauty," and "Ghost&nbsp;
World." In 2019, the actor began playing Mary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:48.900
on the hit AMC show "The Walking Dead," though,&nbsp;
as fans are aware, her character was relegated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:54.420
entirely to the show's tenth season.&nbsp;
While speaking to KTLA 5 in October 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:59.794
Birch revealed that she was not familiar with "The&nbsp;
Walking Dead" prior to joining the series' cast.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.300
"I hadn't watched the show&nbsp;
before I started Season 10,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:08.129
but I went down the rabbit hole immediately and&nbsp;
started like you know, just jamming the seasons."

00:02:08.129 --> 00:02:12.060
The actor then revealed that she found it&nbsp;
difficult to shoot the series due to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:17.396
Atlanta heat – where the show is filmed – but&nbsp;
found the experience rewarding nonetheless.

00:02:17.396 --> 00:02:21.540
"It's a blast because you get to do so many&nbsp;
types of things that normally you don't do."

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:26.580
Since her "Walking Dead" stint, Thora Birch&nbsp;
has only appeared in two subsequent roles:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:31.560
the lead in Oklahoma tornado film "13&nbsp;
Minutes," and as the star of narrative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:36.300
podcast "Overleaper." She's currently&nbsp;
slated to appear in a TV movie based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:41.400
on the real-life story of Gabby Petito — which&nbsp;
she's also directing — as well as the Wednesday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:47.160
Adams TV series "Wednesday." That said, Birch&nbsp;
left "Wednesday" midway into its production.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:52.200
Since she remains credited on six episodes&nbsp;
of the series online, however, it's possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:57.120
that the show's producers will indeed make use of&nbsp;
some of what Birch filmed during her time on-set.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.080
But even if she doesn't show up in&nbsp;
"Wednesday," you can always relive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:05.925
her early career-defining performance&nbsp;
as Dani Dennison in "Hocus Pocus."

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:09.960
"It's been great fun, but&nbsp;
I guess I better be going."

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.820
"Oh, stay for supper."

